{
  "_comment": "Antigravity (agy) permission baseline. Merged by setup.sh into ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json via claude/scripts/agy-apply-permissions.py (that file also holds trustedWorkspaces and per-machine grants, so it is never symlinked). Rules are word-by-word prefixes unless regex:. Precedence: deny > ask > allow. Security model: the terminal sandbox is the boundary (toolPermission=proceed-in-sandbox, enableTerminalSandbox=true). No local tool carries an unsandboxed(...) rule; the only unsandboxed rules are gh read subcommands (git fetch/pull prompt: repo config can name programs for git to run). Reads outside the workspace are served inside the sandbox through allowNonWorkspaceAccess and the read_file(~/...) rules, which the merge script expands to the machine's home. The command deny regexes are defense in depth for sandboxed runs, not a boundary: shell syntax cannot be classified airtight (see the reverted #411).",
  "settings": {
    "toolPermission": "proceed-in-sandbox",
    "enableTerminalSandbox": true,
    "allowNonWorkspaceAccess": true
  },
